# Server (`:server`)

- JVM Ktor only; configure forwarded headers behind Caddy (`X-Forwarded-*`).
- Verify Firebase ID tokens; map to `User` + role; **401/403** for missing/insufficient auth.
- Public routes: only what RGPD allows (consent, no minors public, no internal notes/amounts).
- SQLite: open via `openDatabase()` (WAL + foreign keys on every connection); one-sided relations persisted per data model.
- Schema changes: add a new `server/src/main/sqldelight/migrations/V<n>__<name>.sqm` (never edit an applied one); Flyway applies the generated `.sql` at startup. Prefer additive changes so rollbacks stay possible.
- Validate input at boundaries; consistent JSON error bodies and HTTP status codes.
- No password storage; no blocking work on the Netty event loop — use appropriate dispatchers.
- Koin modules for routes/services/repositories; share DTOs from `:core`.
- Tests in `:server:test` for auth matrix, public filtering, and critical SQL paths.
